# Error Handling (Spring Boot)

Concepts: see `../../patterns/error-handling.mdc`. Below: Spring-specific.

## GlobalExceptionHandler

- @RestControllerAdvice; @ExceptionHandler for specific exceptions; return ResponseEntity with status and body.
- Use ProblemDetail (RFC 7807): set type, title, status, detail, instance, properties; Content-Type application/problem+json.
- Map domain exceptions (e.g. NotFoundException → 404, ValidationException → 400); map AccessDeniedException → 403; generic 500 for unexpected; do not leak stack in prod.

## Result Pattern

- Use Result<T, E> in service layer for expected failures; controller unwraps or maps to ProblemDetail responses.
- Reserve exceptions for unexpected infrastructure/programming failures; let the global handler map those to HTTP.

## Conventions

- Single global handler; consistent ProblemDetail shape; log with correlation ID; appropriate status codes; no stack in response in production.

## Anti-Patterns

- Swallowing exceptions; returning 200 on error; no handler; exposing stack traces; inconsistent error format

